ist for  30th of march 2022. relish the music of  hashem nazum and si mei callumway  bringing her effortless flair to the  screen so some more big praise for oscar  isaac they specifically say he is a  revelation and that moon knight is  dazzling so far these reviews definitely  caught my attention but this next one  isn't so over the top like these others  this is from emily murray from xavi and  she says delivering lots of indiana  jones style archaeology action just swap  out the whip for a cape and oscar  isaac's great turn in the lead role moon  night is plenty of fun it's not as  bonkers as i hoped for but a later  episode hints much more of that is  coming now i believe and i should have  stated this in the beginning that these  critics have seen the first four  episodes of moon night that's a lot of  episodes i don't know how many i'll  personally get i just know i get them  tomorrow but they've seen a good amount  of this series now and even though this  review says it's not as bonkers as she  hoped for that still doesn't mean that  it wasn't really good she still praised  oscar isaac for the lead role and even  compared it to indiana jones which of  course is a win however a lot of the  other reviews are really really good  let's go over to tom power from  techradar and he had a lot to say here  he says it's unlike anything you've seen  from marvel before i'd go as far as to  say and i don't say this lightly it's  the best mcu tv show ever moon knight is  the beneficiary of being completely  untethered from every other mcu project  without those connections wayne if  that's the right word to use it down it  has a freedom to do whatever it wants  and oh boy does it the opening episode  is structured in such a way that but for  the marvel logo at the start you  wouldn't think it's an mcu tv series the  way it's edited  how its narrative plays out isaac's  mesmeric fully present performance  honestly is top tier tv i'll save the  rest for my review there are a couple of  tiny little things there about it just  to put that out there but moon knight is  worth the wait again a review a great  review about moon knight with really  high praise to the series now this one i  really like because it talks about how  different moon knight is from all of the  other mcu projects i've heard a lot of  people and seen a lot of comments in the  comic section talking about how marvel  is releasing so much stuff right now and  while some fans like myself may  absolutely just love that and watch  everything that comes out some might  have to pick and choose what they watch  and it sounds like moon night is just  going to be completely different than  anything we've seen before so i suggest  everybody watching this now some of  these critics have actually mentioned  how weird and actually said the word  horror in their review which i know a  lot of people are going to like tom  percival from bbc radio says had a lot  of fun with moon knight it started weird  and only seems to be getting weirder a  good blend of horror action and humor  plus he has a great cape it's  interesting that he uses the words weird  horror action and humor in the same  paragraph but that's actually kind of  something that i wanted from moon knight  it's kind of a psychological thriller  which i'm actually really excited for  but the fact that it still has some  humor into it is obviously really good  as well the university film review says  moon knight is fantastic and oscar isaac  is exceptional as the tormented mark  spectre this is the marvel show everyone  is going to be talking about completely  bonkers that leads with a haunting  adventure marvel studios has knocked it  out of the park with its best show yet  so a few people have called it bonkers  and weird and now a couple of reviews  have said that it's marvel's best show  yet now right now as it stands loki is  my favorite show followed closely by one  division but based off of these reviews  i am wondering if it's going to stay  that way if my top two are gonna stay  that way after seeing moon night let's  go over to david opie from digital spy  he says i've watched the first four moon  night episodes and i'm as divided by the  show as mark spector himself when it  works it's a wildly original mcu entry  with flashes of greatness but some of  the sillier aspects detract from the  horror die hard comic fans might not  enjoy it as much as newcomers and  honestly that is something that i think  every mcu film or show has had to deal  with because they obviously don't just  copy the comics heck in the miss marvel  trailer yesterday they completely  changed up her powers and that could  piss some people off instead of her  being exposed to the terrigen miss she  gets a bracelet that seemingly gives her  her powers that is completely different  than the comics but if everything went  exactly how it went in the comics we  would already know what would happen and  we'd already know what to expect now  this review does mention the horror  aspect as well however he says that  there are sillier sides that do detract  from that horror aspect now keep in mind  it's kind of like doctor strange the  multiverse of madness yes it's supposed  to be the first horror film in the mcu  but it is still pg-13 and it is still a  marvel slash disney movie the same goes  for moon knight sounds like it's going  to be weird going to be trippy have a  horror aspect to it but it's still going  to be a marvel studios project on disney  plus so don't expect it to be like some  rated r horror film the last review  we'll go over here is from david c james  over at games freezer and he says moon  knight is a very weird show with no  obvious connections to the rest of the  mcu but is all the better for it oscar  isaac rivaling tom hardy for best  regular guy taunted by deep voice  monster that lives in his head  performance another big comparison there  comparing oscar isaac's performance to  tom hardy's as venom and again we get a  mention of how weird it is and how it  doesn't have really any connections to  the mcu now of course i do ultimately  think that they're going to connect moon  knight to the mcu by the end of it i  actually do think moon knight is going  to go on to become an avenger but it  does seem like this is kind of not  necessarily an experiment but  essentially an experiment they're taking  it a very different direction than  anything they've ever done before but i  say it's not an experiment because kevin  feige does everything pretty perfectly  so this could be the future of where  marvel studios is going doing one-off  projects that don't necessarily focus on  that mcu connection but of course are  connected to the mcu so these reviews  seem to be pretty dang good what do you  think about them are you excited for  moon knight and of course once i watch  all of the episodes that i get tomorrow  i'll be sure to give you my initial  thoughts as well and i'm also going to  the premiere on tuesday so i'll probably  vlog that as well but in the meantime  what do you think of these reactions are  you excited for moon knight let me know  your thoughts in the comments down below  don't forget to like the video and  subscribe if you want more marvel videos  for live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof
 

